-- title:
--   Surjectivity criterion for maps from a power series algebra
-- statement:
--   Let $\sigma$ be a finite type, let $\mathcal{O}$ be a commutative ring and let $A$ be a commutative ring which is an $\mathcal{O}$-algebra, local and Noetherian. Let $\varphi \colon \mathcal{O}[[X_i : i \in \sigma]] \to A$ be a homomorphism of $\mathcal{O}$-algebras from the multivariate formal power series algebra, and let $a \colon \sigma \to A$ be a family of elements of $A$ such that $\varphi(X_i) = a_i$ for every $i$ and $a_i$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ for every $i$. Assume further that the composite of the structure map $\mathcal{O} \to A$ with the quotient map $A \to A / I$, where $I$ is the ideal generated by the set of values $\{a_i : i \in \sigma\}$, is surjective, i.e. every element of $A$ is congruent modulo $I$ to the image of an element of $\mathcal{O}$. Then $\varphi$ is surjective. No completeness or separatedness hypothesis is imposed on $A$ beyond its being Noetherian and local.
--
--   This is the surjectivity half of the Cohen-style presentation of a Noetherian local $\mathcal{O}$-algebra as a quotient of a formal power series algebra $\mathcal{O}[[X_1,\dots,X_n]]$, stated purely in commutative-algebraic terms. It underlies the construction of such presentations used later, being cited by [`IsLocalRing.exists_mvPowerSeries_algHom_apply_X_eq_and_surjective_of_span`](thm.html#IsLocalRing.exists_mvPowerSeries_algHom_apply_X_eq_and_surjective_of_span), [`Algebra.exists_presentation_of_residueField`](thm.html#Algebra.exists_presentation_of_residueField) and [`AlgHom.bijective_and_exists_presentation_of_length_cotangent_le`](thm.html#AlgHom.bijective_and_exists_presentation_of_length_cotangent_le).
-- source:
